#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm outperforms all classical algorithms for a query problem, but the advantage is quite modest: one query versus two.\n"
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm extends this advantage — and, in fact, it can be used to solve a couple of different query problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch mengatasi semua algoritma klasik untuk masalah pertanyaan, tetapi kelebihan itu agak sederhana: satu pertanyaan berbanding dua.\n"
"Algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa memperluaskan kelebihan ini — malah, ia boleh digunakan untuk menyelesaikan beberapa masalah pertanyaan yang berbeza.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a quantum circuit description of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"An additional classical post-processing step, not shown in the figure, may also be required depending on the specific problem being solved.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah penerangan Circuit kuantum bagi algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Langkah pemprosesan pasca klasik tambahan, yang tidak ditunjukkan dalam rajah, mungkin juga diperlukan bergantung pada masalah tertentu yang diselesaikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-Jozsa.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-Jozsa.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, we haven't actually discussed what problems this algorithm "
"solves; this is done in the two sections that follow.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudah tentu, kita belum membincangkan masalah apa yang diselesaikan oleh "
"algoritma ini; perkara ini dibincangkan dalam dua bahagian berikutnya.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa problem {#the-deutsch-jozsa-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah Deutsch-Jozsa {#the-deutsch-jozsa-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin with the query problem the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm was "
"originally intended to solve, which is known as the *Deutsch-Jozsa "
"problem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mulakan dengan masalah pertanyaan yang algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa "
"pada asalnya direka untuk diselesaikan, yang dikenali sebagai *masalah "
"Deutsch-Jozsa*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The input function for this problem takes the form $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ for an arbitrary positive integer $n.$\n"
"Like Deutsch's problem, the task is to output $0$ if $f$ is constant and $1$ if $f$ is balanced, which again means that the number of input strings on which the function takes the value $0$ is equal to the number of input strings on which the function takes the value $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi input untuk masalah ini mengambil bentuk $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ untuk integer positif $n$ yang sewenang-wenangnya.\n"
"Seperti masalah Deutsch, tugasnya ialah mengeluarkan $0$ jika $f$ adalah malar dan $1$ jika $f$ adalah seimbang, yang sekali lagi bermakna bilangan rentetan input di mana fungsi mengambil nilai $0$ adalah sama dengan bilangan rentetan input di mana fungsi mengambil nilai $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that, when $n$ is larger than $1,$ there are functions of the form $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ that are neither constant nor balanced.\n"
"For example, the function $f:\\Sigma^2\\rightarrow\\Sigma$ defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa, apabila $n$ lebih besar daripada $1,$ terdapat fungsi berbentuk $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ yang bukan malar mahupun seimbang.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, fungsi $f:\\Sigma^2\\rightarrow\\Sigma$ yang ditakrifkan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(00) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(01) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(10) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(11) & = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(00) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(01) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(10) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(11) & = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"falls into neither of these two categories.\n"
"For the Deutsch-Jozsa problem, we simply don't worry about functions like this — they're considered to be \"don't care\" inputs.\n"
"That is, for this problem we have a *promise* that $f$ is either constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"tidak termasuk dalam mana-mana dua kategori ini.\n"
"Untuk masalah Deutsch-Jozsa, kita tidak perlu risau tentang fungsi seperti ini — ia dianggap sebagai input \"jangan ambil pusing\".\n"
"Iaitu, untuk masalah ini kita ada *janji* bahawa $f$ sama ada malar atau seimbang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch-Jozsa problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promise: $f$ is either constant or balanced \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah Deutsch-Jozsa\">\n"
"Input: fungsi $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Janji: $f$ sama ada malar atau seimbang \\\n"
"Output: $0$ jika $f$ malar, $1$ jika $f$ seimbang\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, with its single query, solves this problem in the following sense:\n"
"if every one of the $n$ measurement outcomes is $0,$ then the function $f$ is constant;\n"
"and otherwise, if at least one of the measurement outcomes is $1,$ then the function $f$ is balanced.\n"
"Another way to say this is that the circuit described above is followed by a classical post-processing step in which the OR of the measurement outcomes is computed to produce the output.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa, dengan satu pertanyaannya, menyelesaikan masalah ini dalam erti kata berikut:\n"
"jika setiap satu daripada $n$ hasil ukuran adalah $0,$ maka fungsi $f$ adalah malar;\n"
"dan sebaliknya, jika sekurang-kurangnya satu hasil ukuran adalah $1,$ maka fungsi $f$ adalah seimbang.\n"
"Cara lain untuk menyatakannya ialah Circuit yang dihuraikan di atas diikuti dengan langkah pemprosesan pasca klasik di mana OR bagi hasil ukuran dikira untuk menghasilkan output.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm analysis {#algorithm-analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis algoritma {#algorithm-analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze the performance of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem, it's helpful to begin by thinking about the action of a single layer of Hadamard gates.\n"
"A Hadamard operation can be expressed as a matrix in the usual way,\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis prestasi algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa bagi masalah Deutsch-Jozsa, adalah berguna untuk memulakan dengan memikirkan tindakan satu lapisan gate Hadamard.\n"
"Operasi Hadamard boleh dinyatakan sebagai matriks dengan cara biasa,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"but we can also express this operation in terms of its action on standard "
"basis states:\n"
msgstr ""
"tetapi kita juga boleh menyatakan operasi ini dari segi tindakannya pada "
"keadaan asas piawai:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"H \\vert 0\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[3mm]\n"
"H \\vert 1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"H \\vert 0\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[3mm]\n"
"H \\vert 1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "These two equations can be combined into a single formula,\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-dua persamaan ini boleh digabungkan menjadi satu formula tunggal,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H \\vert a \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (-1)^a \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{b\\in\\{0,1\\}} (-1)^{ab} \\vert b\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H \\vert a \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (-1)^a \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{b\\in\\{0,1\\}} (-1)^{ab} \\vert b\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which is true for both choices of $a\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
msgstr "yang berlaku untuk kedua-dua pilihan $a\\in\\Sigma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now suppose that instead of just a single qubit we have $n$ qubits, and a Hadamard operation is performed on each.\n"
"The combined operation on the $n$ qubits is described by the tensor product $H\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H$ ($n$ times), which we write as $H^{\\otimes n}$ for conciseness and clarity.\n"
"Using the formula from above, followed by expanding and then simplifying, we can express the action of this combined operation on the standard basis states of $n$ qubits like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang andaikan bahawa bukannya hanya satu qubit kita mempunyai $n$ qubit, dan operasi Hadamard dilakukan pada setiap satu.\n"
"Operasi gabungan pada $n$ qubit dihuraikan oleh hasil darab tensor $H\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H$ ($n$ kali), yang kita tulis sebagai $H^{\\otimes n}$ untuk keringkasan dan kejelasan.\n"
"Menggunakan formula di atas, diikuti dengan mengembangkan dan kemudian memudahkan, kita boleh menyatakan tindakan operasi gabungan ini pada keadaan asas piawai bagi $n$ qubit seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_1 x_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\bigl(H \\vert x_{n-1} \\rangle \\bigr) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\bigl(H \\vert x_{0} \\rangle \\bigr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{n-1} y_{n-1}} \\vert y_{n-1} \\rangle \\Biggr)\n"
"  \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\n"
"  \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{0}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{0} y_{0}} \\vert y_{0} \\rangle \\Biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"  (-1)^{x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0} \\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_1 x_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\bigl(H \\vert x_{n-1} \\rangle \\bigr) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\bigl(H \\vert x_{0} \\rangle \\bigr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{n-1} y_{n-1}} \\vert y_{n-1} \\rangle \\Biggr)\n"
"  \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\n"
"  \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{0}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{0} y_{0}} \\vert y_{0} \\rangle \\Biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"  (-1)^{x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0} \\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, by the way, we're writing binary strings of length $n$ as "
"$x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ and $y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0,$ following Qiskit's indexing "
"convention.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita menulis rentetan binari panjang $n$ sebagai $x_{n-1}\\cdots "
"x_0$ dan $y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0,$ mengikut konvensyen pengindeksan Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula provides us with a useful tool for analyzing the quantum circuit above.\n"
"After the first layer of Hadamard gates is performed, the state of the $n+1$ qubits (including the leftmost/bottom qubit, which is treated separately from the rest) is\n"
msgstr ""
"Formula ini memberi kita alat yang berguna untuk menganalisis Circuit kuantum di atas.\n"
"Selepas lapisan gate Hadamard pertama dilakukan, keadaan $n+1$ qubit (termasuk qubit paling kiri/bawah, yang dirawat secara berasingan daripada yang lain) ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl( H \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0 \\cdots 0 \\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl( H \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0 \\cdots 0 \\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When the $U_f$ operation is performed, this state is transformed into\n"
msgstr "Apabila operasi $U_f$ dilakukan, keadaan ini berubah menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"through exactly the same phase kick-back phenomenon that we saw in the "
"analysis of Deutsch's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"melalui fenomena tendangan fasa yang sama seperti yang kita lihat dalam "
"analisis algoritma Deutsch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then the second layer of Hadamard gates is performed, which (by the formula "
"above) transforms this state into\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian lapisan gate Hadamard kedua dilakukan, yang (melalui formula di "
"atas) mengubah keadaan ini menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"\\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) + x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0}\n"
"\\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"\\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) + x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0}\n"
"\\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This expression looks somewhat complicated, and not too much can be "
"concluded about the probabilities to obtain different measurement outcomes "
"without knowing more about the function $f.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ungkapan ini kelihatan agak rumit, dan tidak banyak yang boleh disimpulkan "
"tentang kebarangkalian mendapat hasil ukuran yang berbeza tanpa mengetahui "
"lebih lanjut tentang fungsi $f.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fortunately, all we need to know is the probability that every one of the measurement outcomes is $0$ — because that's the probability that the algorithm determines that $f$ is constant.\n"
"This probability has a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nasib baik, yang perlu kita ketahui hanyalah kebarangkalian bahawa setiap satu hasil ukuran adalah $0$ — kerana itulah kebarangkalian algoritma menentukan bahawa $f$ adalah malar.\n"
"Kebarangkalian ini mempunyai formula yang mudah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl\\vert\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)}\n"
"\\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $f$ is constant}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\text{if $f$ is balanced}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl\\vert\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)}\n"
"\\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $f$ is constant}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\text{if $f$ is balanced}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, if $f$ is constant, then either $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 0$ for every string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0,$\n"
"in which case the value of the sum is $2^n,$ or $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 1$ for every string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0,$\n"
"in which case the value of the sum is $-2^n.$\n"
"Dividing by $2^n$ and taking the square of the absolute value yields $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lebih terperinci, jika $f$ adalah malar, maka sama ada $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 0$ untuk setiap rentetan $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0,$\n"
"dalam kes ini nilai jumlah ialah $2^n,$ atau $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 1$ untuk setiap rentetan $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0,$\n"
"dalam kes ini nilai jumlah ialah $-2^n.$\n"
"Membahagi dengan $2^n$ dan mengambil kuasa dua nilai mutlak menghasilkan $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If, on the other hand, $f$ is balanced, then $f$ takes the value $0$ on half"
" of the strings $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ and the value $1$ on the other half, so"
" the $+1$ terms and $-1$ terms in the sum cancel and we're left with the "
"value $0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, jika $f$ adalah seimbang, maka $f$ mengambil nilai $0$ pada "
"separuh rentetan $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ dan nilai $1$ pada separuh yang lain, "
"jadi sebutan $+1$ dan sebutan $-1$ dalam jumlah saling menghapuskan dan kita"
" mendapat nilai $0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We conclude that the algorithm operates correctly provided that the promise "
"is fulfilled.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita menyimpulkan bahawa algoritma beroperasi dengan betul selagi janji "
"dipenuhi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty}"
msgstr "Kesukaran klasik {#classical-difficulty}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm works every time, always giving us the correct answer when the promise is met, and requires a single query.\n"
"How does this compare with classical query algorithms for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem?\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa berfungsi setiap masa, sentiasa memberi jawapan yang betul apabila janji dipenuhi, dan memerlukan satu pertanyaan sahaja.\n"
"Bagaimana ini berbanding dengan algoritma pertanyaan klasik untuk masalah Deutsch-Jozsa?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, any *deterministic* classical algorithm that correctly solves the Deutsch-Jozsa problem must make exponentially many queries:\n"
"$2^{n-1} + 1$ queries are required in the worst case.\n"
"The reasoning is that, if a deterministic algorithm queries $f$ on $2^{n-1}$ or fewer different strings, and obtains the same function value every time, then both answers are still possible.\n"
"The function might be constant, or it might be balanced but through bad luck the queries all happen to return the same function value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, mana-mana algoritma klasik *deterministik* yang menyelesaikan masalah Deutsch-Jozsa dengan betul mesti membuat pertanyaan yang amat banyak:\n"
"$2^{n-1} + 1$ pertanyaan diperlukan dalam kes terburuk.\n"
"Alasannya ialah, jika algoritma deterministik membuat pertanyaan $f$ pada $2^{n-1}$ atau lebih sedikit rentetan berbeza, dan mendapat nilai fungsi yang sama setiap kali, maka kedua-dua jawapan masih mungkin.\n"
"Fungsi itu mungkin malar, atau ia mungkin seimbang tetapi malangnya semua pertanyaan kebetulan mengembalikan nilai fungsi yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second possibility might seem unlikely — but for deterministic algorithms there's no randomness or uncertainty, so they will fail systematically on certain functions.\n"
"We therefore have a significant advantage of quantum over classical algorithms in this regard.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemungkinan kedua mungkin kelihatan tidak mungkin — tetapi untuk algoritma deterministik tiada kerawakan atau ketidaktentuan, jadi mereka akan gagal secara sistematik pada fungsi tertentu.\n"
"Oleh itu kita mempunyai kelebihan yang ketara bagi kuantum berbanding algoritma klasik dalam hal ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is a catch, however, which is that *probabilistic* classical algorithms can solve the Deutsch-Jozsa problem with very high probability using just a few queries.\n"
"In particular, if we simply choose a few different strings of length $n$ randomly, and query $f$ on those strings, it's unlikely that we'll get the same function value for all of them when $f$ is balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, terdapat satu tangkapan, iaitu algoritma klasik *kebarangkalian* boleh menyelesaikan masalah Deutsch-Jozsa dengan kebarangkalian yang sangat tinggi menggunakan hanya beberapa pertanyaan sahaja.\n"
"Khususnya, jika kita hanya memilih beberapa rentetan berbeza panjang $n$ secara rawak, dan membuat pertanyaan $f$ pada rentetan tersebut, tidak mungkin kita mendapat nilai fungsi yang sama untuk semua daripadanya apabila $f$ adalah seimbang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be specific, if we choose $k$ input strings $x^1,\\ldots,x^k \\in \\Sigma^n$ uniformly at random, evaluate $f(x^1),\\ldots,f(x^k),$ and answer $0$ if the function values are all the same, and $1$ if not, then we'll always be correct when $f$ is constant, and wrong in the case that $f$ is balanced with probability just $2^{-k + 1}.$\n"
"If we take $k = 11,$ for instance, this algorithm will answer correctly with probability greater than $99.9$%.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih spesifik, jika kita memilih $k$ rentetan input $x^1,\\ldots,x^k \\in \\Sigma^n$ secara seragam rawak, menilai $f(x^1),\\ldots,f(x^k),$ dan menjawab $0$ jika nilai fungsi semuanya sama, dan $1$ jika tidak, maka kita akan sentiasa betul apabila $f$ adalah malar, dan salah dalam kes $f$ seimbang dengan kebarangkalian hanya $2^{-k + 1}.$\n"
"Jika kita ambil $k = 11,$ sebagai contoh, algoritma ini akan menjawab dengan betul dengan kebarangkalian lebih daripada $99.9$%.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this reason, we do still have a rather modest advantage of quantum over "
"classical algorithms — but it is nevertheless a quantifiable advantage "
"representing an improvement over Deutsch's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Atas sebab ini, kita masih mempunyai kelebihan yang agak sederhana bagi "
"kuantum berbanding algoritma klasik — tetapi ia tetap merupakan kelebihan "
"yang boleh diukur yang menunjukkan peningkatan berbanding algoritma "
"Deutsch.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch-Jozsa with Qiskit {#deutsch-jozsa-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "Deutsch-Jozsa dengan Qiskit {#deutsch-jozsa-with-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm in Qiskit, we'll start by defining a function `dj_query` that generates a quantum circuit implementing a query gate, for a randomly selected function satisfying the promise for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem.\n"
"With a 50% chance, the function is constant, and with 50% change the function is balanced.\n"
"For each of those two possibilities, the function is selected uniformly from the functions of that type.\n"
"The argument is the number of input bits of the function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk melaksanakan algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa dalam Qiskit, kita akan mulakan dengan mentakrifkan fungsi `dj_query` yang menjana Circuit kuantum yang melaksanakan gate pertanyaan, untuk fungsi yang dipilih secara rawak yang memenuhi janji untuk masalah Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Dengan kebarangkalian 50%, fungsi adalah malar, dan dengan kebarangkalian 50% fungsi adalah seimbang.\n"
"Untuk setiap dua kemungkinan tersebut, fungsi dipilih secara seragam daripada fungsi-fungsi jenis itu.\n"
"Argumen ialah bilangan bit input bagi fungsi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can show the quantum circuit implementation of the query gate using the "
"`draw` method as usual.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh menunjukkan pelaksanaan Circuit kuantum bagi gate pertanyaan "
"menggunakan kaedah `draw` seperti biasa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/b4a6df3d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/b4a6df3d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we define a function that creates the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit, taking a "
"quantum circuit implementation of a query gate as an argument.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya kita takrifkan fungsi yang mencipta Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa, "
"mengambil pelaksanaan Circuit kuantum bagi gate pertanyaan sebagai "
"argumen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, a function that runs the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit once is defined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, fungsi yang menjalankan Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa sekali "
"ditakrifkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can test our implementation by choosing a function randomly, displaying "
"the quantum circuit implementation of a query gate for this function, and "
"then running the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm on that function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh menguji pelaksanaan kita dengan memilih fungsi secara rawak, "
"memaparkan pelaksanaan Circuit kuantum bagi gate pertanyaan untuk fungsi "
"ini, dan kemudian menjalankan algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa pada fungsi "
"tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/aca4745e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/aca4745e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Bernstein-Vazirani problem {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah Bernstein-Vazirani {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we'll discuss a problem known as the *Bernstein-Vazirani problem*.\n"
"It's also called the *Fourier sampling problem*, although there are more general formulations of this problem that also go by that name.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, kita akan bincangkan satu masalah yang dikenali sebagai *masalah Bernstein-Vazirani*.\n"
"Ia juga dipanggil *masalah pensampelan Fourier*, walaupun terdapat rumusan yang lebih umum bagi masalah ini yang turut menggunakan nama tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's introduce some notation.\n"
"For any two binary strings $x = x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0$ and $y = y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$ of length $n,$ we define\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, mari kita perkenalkan sedikit notasi.\n"
"Untuk mana-mana dua rentetan binari $x = x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0$ dan $y = y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$ dengan panjang $n,$ kita takrifkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y = x_{n-1} y_{n-1} \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus x_0 y_0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y = x_{n-1} y_{n-1} \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus x_0 y_0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll refer to this operation as the *binary dot product*.\n"
"An alternative way to define it is like so.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan merujuk operasi ini sebagai *hasil darab titik binari*.\n"
"Cara alternatif untuk mentakrifkannya adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is odd}\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"0 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is even}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ adalah ganjil}\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"0 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ adalah genap}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that this is a symmetric operation, meaning that the result doesn't change if we swap $x$ and $y,$ so we're free to do that whenever it's convenient.\n"
"Sometimes it's useful to think about the binary dot product $x \\cdot y$ as being the parity of the bits of $x$ in positions where the string $y$ has a $1,$ or equivalently, the parity of the bits of $y$ in positions where the string $x$ has a $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa ini adalah operasi simetri, bermakna hasilnya tidak berubah jika kita tukarkan $x$ dan $y,$ jadi kita bebas berbuat demikian bila-bila masa perlu.\n"
"Kadang-kadang berguna untuk memikirkan hasil darab titik binari $x \\cdot y$ sebagai pariti bit-bit dalam $x$ pada kedudukan di mana rentetan $y$ mempunyai $1,$ atau secara setara, pariti bit-bit dalam $y$ pada kedudukan di mana rentetan $x$ mempunyai $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this notation in hand we can now define the Bernstein-Vazirani "
"problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan notasi ini, kita kini boleh mentakrifkan masalah Bernstein-"
"Vazirani.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Bernstein-Vazirani problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promise: there exists a binary string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ for which $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ for all $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: the string $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah Bernstein-Vazirani\">\n"
"Input: suatu fungsi $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Janji: wujud rentetan binari $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ di mana $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ untuk semua $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: rentetan $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We don't actually need a new quantum algorithm for this problem; the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm solves it.\n"
"In the interest of clarity, let's refer to the quantum circuit from above, which doesn't include the classical post-processing step of computing the OR, as the *Deutsch-Jozsa circuit*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sebenarnya tidak memerlukan algoritma kuantum baharu untuk masalah ini; algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa menyelesaikannya.\n"
"Demi kejelasan, mari kita rujuk Circuit kuantum di atas, yang tidak merangkumi langkah pasca-pemprosesan klasik untuk mengira OR, sebagai *Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm analysis {#algorithm-analysis-1}"
msgstr "Analisis algoritma {#algorithm-analysis-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze how the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit works for a function satisfying the promise for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, we'll begin with a quick observation.\n"
"Using the binary dot product, we can alternatively describe the action of $n$ Hadamard gates on the standard basis states of $n$ qubits as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis cara Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa berfungsi bagi fungsi yang memenuhi janji masalah Bernstein-Vazirani, kita akan mulakan dengan satu pemerhatian ringkas.\n"
"Menggunakan hasil darab titik binari, kita boleh menerangkan secara alternatif tindakan $n$ gate Hadamard ke atas keadaan asas piawai bagi $n$ qubit seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we saw when analyzing Deutsch's algorithm, this is because "
"the value $(-1)^k$ for any integer $k$ depends only on whether $k$ is even "
"or odd.\n"
msgstr ""
"Serupa dengan apa yang kita lihat semasa menganalisis algoritma Deutsch, ini"
" kerana nilai $(-1)^k$ untuk mana-mana integer $k$ hanya bergantung pada "
"sama ada $k$ genap atau ganjil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Turning to the Deutsch–Jozsa circuit, after the first layer of Hadamard "
"gates is performed, the state of the $n+1$ qubits is\n"
msgstr ""
"Beralih kepada Circuit Deutsch–Jozsa, selepas lapisan pertama gate Hadamard "
"dilakukan, keadaan $n+1$ qubit adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The query gate is then performed, which (through the phase kickback "
"phenomenon) transforms the state into\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate kueri kemudian dilakukan, yang (melalui fenomena tendangan fasa) "
"mengubah keadaan kepada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using our formula for the action of a layer of Hadamard gates, we see that "
"the second layer of Hadamard gates then transforms this state into\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan rumus kita untuk tindakan lapisan gate Hadamard, kita dapati "
"bahawa lapisan kedua gate Hadamard kemudian mengubah keadaan ini kepada\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x) + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x) + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can make some simplifications, in the exponent of $-1$ inside the sum.\n"
"We're promised that $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ for some string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0,$ so we can express the state as\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini kita boleh membuat beberapa penyederhanaan pada eksponen $-1$ di dalam jumlah.\n"
"Kita dijanjikan bahawa $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ untuk rentetan tertentu $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0,$ jadi kita boleh ungkapkan keadaan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{s\\cdot x + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{s\\cdot x + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $s\\cdot x$ and $x\\cdot y$ are binary values, we can replace the addition with the exclusive-OR — again because the only thing that matters for an integer in the exponent of $-1$ is whether it is even or odd.\n"
"Making use of the symmetry of the binary dot product, we obtain this expression for the state:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kerana $s\\cdot x$ dan $x\\cdot y$ adalah nilai binari, kita boleh menggantikan penambahan dengan eksklusif-OR — sekali lagi kerana satu-satunya perkara yang penting bagi integer dalam eksponen $-1$ adalah sama ada ia genap atau ganjil.\n"
"Menggunakan simetri hasil darab titik binari, kita memperoleh ungkapan ini untuk keadaan tersebut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Parentheses have been added for clarity, though they aren't really "
"necessary because it's conventional to treat the binary dot product as "
"having higher precedence than the exclusive-OR.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Kurungan telah ditambah untuk kejelasan, walaupun ia tidak benar-benar "
"diperlukan kerana adalah konvensional untuk memperlakukan hasil darab titik "
"binari sebagai mempunyai keutamaan lebih tinggi daripada eksklusif-OR.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "At this point we will make use of the following formula.\n"
msgstr "Pada ketika ini kita akan menggunakan rumus berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x) = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x) = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can obtain the formula through a similar formula for bits,\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh memperoleh rumus ini melalui rumus serupa untuk bit,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(a c) \\oplus (b c) = (a \\oplus b) c,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(a c) \\oplus (b c) = (a \\oplus b) c,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"together with an expansion of the binary dot product and bitwise exclusive-"
"OR:\n"
msgstr ""
"bersama-sama dengan pengembangan hasil darab titik binari dan eksklusif-OR "
"bitwise:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} x_{n-1}) \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} x_{0}) \\oplus\n"
"(y_{n-1} x_{n-1})  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (y_{0} x_{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} \\oplus y_{n-1}) x_{n-1}  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} \\oplus y_{0}) x_{0} \\\\\n"
"& = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} x_{n-1}) \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} x_{0}) \\oplus\n"
"(y_{n-1} x_{n-1})  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (y_{0} x_{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} \\oplus y_{n-1}) x_{n-1}  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} \\oplus y_{0}) x_{0} \\\\\n"
"& = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This allows us to express the state of the circuit immediately prior to the "
"measurements like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini membolehkan kita mengungkapkan keadaan Circuit sejurus sebelum "
"pengukuran seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The final step is to make use of yet another formula, which works for every "
"binary string $z = z_{n-1}\\cdots z_0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah terakhir adalah menggunakan satu lagi rumus, yang berlaku untuk "
"setiap rentetan binari $z = z_{n-1}\\cdots z_0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{z \\cdot x}\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $z = 0^n$}\\\\\n"
"0 & \\text{if $z\\neq 0^n$}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{z \\cdot x}\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{jika $z = 0^n$}\\\\\n"
"0 & \\text{jika $z\\neq 0^n$}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're using a simple notation for strings that we'll use several more "
"times in the lesson: $0^n$ is the all-zero string of length $n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita menggunakan notasi ringkas untuk rentetan yang akan kita "
"gunakan beberapa kali lagi dalam pelajaran ini: $0^n$ adalah rentetan semua-"
"sifar dengan panjang $n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple way to argue that this formula works is to consider the two cases separately.\n"
"If $z = 0^n,$ then $z\\cdot x = 0$ for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ so the value of each term in the sum is $1,$ and we obtain $1$ by summing and dividing by $2^n.$\n"
"On the other hand, if any one of the bits of $z$ is equal to $1,$ then the binary dot product $z\\cdot x$ is equal to $0$ for exactly half of the possible choices for $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ and $1$ for the other half — because the value of the binary dot product $z\\cdot x$ flips (from $0$ to $1$ or from $1$ to $0$) if we flip any bit of $x$ in a position where $z$ has a $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara mudah untuk membuktikan bahawa rumus ini betul adalah dengan mempertimbangkan dua kes secara berasingan.\n"
"Jika $z = 0^n,$ maka $z\\cdot x = 0$ untuk setiap rentetan $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ jadi nilai setiap sebutan dalam jumlah adalah $1,$ dan kita mendapat $1$ selepas menjumlah dan membahagi dengan $2^n.$\n"
"Sebaliknya, jika mana-mana satu bit dalam $z$ adalah sama dengan $1,$ maka hasil darab titik binari $z\\cdot x$ adalah sama dengan $0$ untuk tepat separuh daripada pilihan yang mungkin bagi $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ dan $1$ untuk separuh yang lain — kerana nilai hasil darab titik binari $z\\cdot x$ bertukar (dari $0$ ke $1$ atau dari $1$ ke $0$) jika kita tukarkan mana-mana bit dalam $x$ pada kedudukan di mana $z$ mempunyai $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we now apply this formula to simplify the state of the circuit prior to "
"the measurements, we obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita kini menerapkan rumus ini untuk menyederhanakan keadaan Circuit "
"sebelum pengukuran, kita peroleh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert s \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert s \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"owing to the fact that $s\\oplus y = 0^n$ if and only if $y = s.$\n"
"Thus, the measurements reveal precisely the string $s$ we're looking for.\n"
msgstr ""
"kerana $s\\oplus y = 0^n$ jika dan hanya jika $y = s.$\n"
"Oleh itu, pengukuran mendedahkan tepat rentetan $s$ yang kita cari.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty-1}"
msgstr "Kesukaran klasik {#classical-difficulty-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit solves the Bernstein-Vazirani problem with a"
" single query, any classical query algorithm must make at least $n$ queries "
"to solve this problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa menyelesaikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani "
"dengan satu kueri, mana-mana algoritma kueri klasik mesti membuat sekurang-"
"kurangnya $n$ kueri untuk menyelesaikan masalah ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be reasoned through a so-called *information theoretic* argument, which is very simple in this case.\n"
"Each classical query reveals a single bit of information about the solution, and there are $n$ bits of information that need to be uncovered — so at least $n$ queries are needed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini boleh dibuktikan melalui hujah yang dipanggil *teori maklumat*, yang sangat mudah dalam kes ini.\n"
"Setiap kueri klasik mendedahkan satu bit maklumat tentang penyelesaian, dan terdapat $n$ bit maklumat yang perlu diungkap — jadi sekurang-kurangnya $n$ kueri diperlukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, in fact, possible to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem classically by querying the function on each of the $n$ strings having a single $1,$ in each possible position, and $0$ for all other bits, which reveals the bits of $s$ one at a time.\n"
"Therefore, the advantage of quantum over classical algorithms for this problem is $1$ query versus $n$ queries.\n"
msgstr ""
"Malah, adalah mungkin untuk menyelesaikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani secara klasik dengan membuat kueri terhadap fungsi pada setiap $n$ rentetan yang mempunyai satu $1$ sahaja, pada setiap kedudukan yang mungkin, dan $0$ untuk semua bit lain, yang mendedahkan bit-bit dalam $s$ satu demi satu.\n"
"Oleh itu, kelebihan kuantum berbanding algoritma klasik untuk masalah ini adalah $1$ kueri berbanding $n$ kueri.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bernstein-Vazirani with Qiskit {#bernstein-vazirani-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "Bernstein-Vazirani dengan Qiskit {#bernstein-vazirani-with-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've already implemented the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit above, and here we will make use of it to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem.\n"
"First we'll define a function that implements a query gate for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem given any binary string $s.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita telah pun melaksanakan Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa di atas, dan di sini kita akan menggunakannya untuk menyelesaikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani.\n"
"Pertama, kita akan takrifkan fungsi yang melaksanakan gate kueri untuk masalah Bernstein-Vazirani bagi mana-mana rentetan binari $s.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/11861a7e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/11861a7e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can create a function that runs the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit on the "
"function, using the `compile_circuit` function that was defined "
"previously.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini kita boleh mencipta fungsi yang menjalankan Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa ke "
"atas fungsi tersebut, menggunakan fungsi `compile_circuit` yang telah "
"ditakrifkan sebelum ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remark on nomenclature {#remark-on-nomenclature}"
msgstr "Catatan tentang penamaan {#remark-on-nomenclature}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, it is common that the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm is referred to as the \"Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm.\"\n"
"This is slightly misleading, because the algorithm *is* the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, as Bernstein and Vazirani were very clear about in their work.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam konteks masalah Bernstein-Vazirani, adalah lazim bahawa algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa dirujuk sebagai \"algoritma Bernstein-Vazirani.\"\n"
"Ini sedikit mengelirukan, kerana algoritmanya *memang* algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa, seperti yang dinyatakan dengan jelas oleh Bernstein dan Vazirani dalam karya mereka.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Bernstein and Vazirani did after showing that the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm solves the Bernstein-Vazirani problem (as it is stated above) was to define a much more complicated problem, known as the *recursive Fourier sampling problem*.\n"
"This is a highly contrived problem where solutions to different instances of the problem effectively unlock new levels of the problem arranged in a tree-like structure.\n"
"The Bernstein-Vazirani problem is essentially just the base case of this more complicated problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apa yang Bernstein dan Vazirani lakukan setelah menunjukkan bahawa algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa menyelesaikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani (seperti yang dinyatakan di atas) adalah mentakrifkan satu masalah yang jauh lebih rumit, dikenali sebagai *masalah pensampelan Fourier rekursif*.\n"
"Ini adalah masalah yang sangat direka-bentuk di mana penyelesaian kepada contoh-contoh masalah yang berbeza secara efektif membuka tahap-tahap baharu masalah yang disusun dalam struktur seperti pokok.\n"
"Masalah Bernstein-Vazirani pada dasarnya hanyalah kes asas bagi masalah yang lebih rumit ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The recursive Fourier sampling problem was the first known example of a query problem where quantum algorithms have a so-called *super-polynomial* advantage over probabilistic algorithms, thereby surpassing the advantage of quantum over classical offered by the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"Intuitively speaking, the recursive version of the problem amplifies the $1$ versus $n$ advantage of quantum algorithms to something much larger.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah pensampelan Fourier rekursif adalah contoh pertama yang diketahui bagi masalah kueri di mana algoritma kuantum mempunyai kelebihan yang dipanggil *super-polinomial* berbanding algoritma probabilistik, dengan itu melampaui kelebihan kuantum berbanding klasik yang ditawarkan oleh algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Secara intuitif, versi rekursif masalah ini memperkuatkan kelebihan $1$ berbanding $n$ bagi algoritma kuantum kepada sesuatu yang jauh lebih besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most challenging aspect of the mathematical analysis establishing this advantage is showing that classical query algorithms can't solve the problem without making lots of queries.\n"
"This is quite typical; for many problems it can be very difficult to rule out creative classical approaches that solve them efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aspek paling mencabar dalam analisis matematik yang membuktikan kelebihan ini adalah menunjukkan bahawa algoritma kueri klasik tidak dapat menyelesaikan masalah tersebut tanpa membuat banyak kueri.\n"
"Ini cukup tipikal; untuk banyak masalah, boleh jadi sangat sukar untuk menolak pendekatan klasik yang kreatif yang menyelesaikannya dengan cekap.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simon's problem, and the algorithm for it described in the next section, does provide a much simpler example of a super-polynomial (and, in fact, exponential) advantage of quantum over classical algorithms, and for this reason the recursive Fourier sampling problem is less often discussed.\n"
"It is, nevertheless, an interesting computational problem in its own right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah Simon, dan algoritma untuknya yang diterangkan dalam bahagian seterusnya, memang memberikan contoh yang jauh lebih mudah tentang kelebihan super-polinomial (dan, sebenarnya, eksponen) kuantum berbanding algoritma klasik, dan atas sebab ini masalah pensampelan Fourier rekursif kurang kerap dibincangkan.\n"
"Ia tetap merupakan masalah pengiraan yang menarik dengan sendirinya.\n"
